fix(skills): source skillDispatchName from baseConfig, not parent ctx

Codex review caught that both Fix A and Fix B in fork-child-config.ts
read `ctx.skillDispatchName` (the PARENT executor's context) instead of
`baseConfig.skillDispatchName` (the CURRENT fork's identity set by
fork-dispatch.ts:156,251). For a top-level skill dispatch the parent's
ctx has no skillDispatchName, so the execution guard and propagation
were both no-ops at the first fork level — exactly the level where the
recursive call fires.

Source from `baseConfig.skillDispatchName` at both sites so the guard
activates at depth 1 (the fork itself) and propagates from depth 2+.
